# tools/taxonomy.sh: the SDK's PascalCase names that are neither Bevy's nor a deprecated alias, a reason each.
# web NAME   reason: the web's (HTML, CSS, React) name for it
# raea NAME  reason: raea's own, with no Bevy or web name to take

# the web's: HTML's elements, and Tone.js's names (the web's audio library, whose API /tone keeps)
web Audio            HTML's <audio>: sound in step with the frame
web Img              HTML's <img>: the renderer holds the frame until it has loaded
web Video            HTML's <video>: a clip in step with the frame
web OffscreenCanvas  the web's OffscreenCanvas: a canvas no page shows, its 2D context measured and read back (layout-reads LR6)
web Tone             Tone.js as a namespace (import * as Tone), as its users write it
web Loop             Tone.js's Loop: a callback every interval in transport time
web Part             Tone.js's Part: values at times
web Sequence         Tone.js's Sequence: one value per subdivision

# raea's own: the video timeline (no Bevy concept; frame-addressed pieces of a composition)
raea AbsoluteFill    a box over its parent, as a flex column: the page layer's full-frame container
raea Composition     a composition declared in the root (id, size, fps, length), found by registerRoot
raea Series          shots one after another on the timeline
raea Freeze          its children held at one frame
raea Nudge           its child moved in front of its own transform
raea Effect          a look (blur, black and white, sepia and more) on everything drawn under it, for its part's frames
raea Transition      its child coming in over its part's first frames and going out over its last
raea Overlay         children only in a render asked for that overlay
raea Region          a box at a named band, clear of the face perception found
raea InputRegion     a box that keeps a press until it's let go (a panel's page of its own)
raea Clock           the tree at one frame of a composition (the frame's provider)
raea Matchmove       footage with solved 3D standing in it (its own Canvas3D)
raea Plate           footage behind the 3D, filling the camera's view

# raea's own: motion (frame-pure animation, engine/animate)
raea Animate         a frame-pure animation of its child (raea_core_animate's Animation)
raea Stagger         Animate over children, each delayed
raea Easing          the easing curves (in, out, inOut), as values

# raea's own: sound beyond Bevy's (raea-runtime-sound: seedling, speech, songs)
raea Seedling        bevy_seedling's mixer graph as TSX (the crate's name: no single Bevy type)
raea Sound3D         a sound placed in the 3D, heard from the camera (seedling's spatial sampler)
raea Speech          a line spoken by the narration voice, word-timed
raea SongPlot        a song's energy map drawn for a human to check

# raea's own: 3D pieces with no single Bevy type (each groups several, its @bevy tags name them)
raea AntiAliasing    one choice over Bevy's Smaa, Fxaa, TemporalAntiAliasing and Msaa
raea AmbientOcclusion Bevy's ScreenSpaceAmbientOcclusion with its quality and thickness (M5: ScreenSpaceAmbientOcclusion)
raea Shadows         the shadow maps' settings together (PointLightShadowMap, filtering, cascades)
raea Grade           Bevy's ColorGrading with chromatic aberration and the effect stack (ColorGrading alone is M5's name)
raea Fog             Bevy's DistanceFog plus an exponential form by density (DistanceFog is M5's name)
raea ToneMapping     Bevy's Tonemapping with Exposure (Tonemapping is M5's name)
raea Environment     Bevy's EnvironmentMapLight from a panorama, drawn as the sky with `background` (M5: EnvironmentMapLight)
raea Decal           Bevy's ForwardDecal with its picture and the camera's depth prepass (M5: ForwardDecal)
raea Look            the scene's one look (paint, toon, flat) as an ExtendedMaterial on every surface
raea SurfaceShader   one WGSL/WESL surface for every material in the scene (docs/shaders.feature SH4)
raea ShaderMesh      a mesh drawn by its own shader, uniforms set at load (Mesh3d with a raea Material)
web ThreeShaderMaterial  three.js's ShaderMaterial (GLSL) or node material (WGSL) as it is, run by raea's engine (docs/r3f.feature R3F11)
raea FramePass       a full-screen pass over the camera's frame (docs/shaders.feature)
raea Compute         a compute shader run once a frame before the cameras draw (docs/shaders.feature SH10)
raea ShaderExtension raea's MaterialExtension running a surface shader (ExtendedMaterial's extension)
raea GridExtension   raea's MaterialExtension drawing a grid (ExtendedMaterial's extension)
raea PaintExtension  raea's MaterialExtension for the paint look (ExtendedMaterial's extension)
raea WearExtension  raea's MaterialExtension that chips, grimes and rusts a StandardMaterial in the part's own space (systems/wear); Bevy has none
raea ProceduralExtension  raea's MaterialExtension that draws wood, stone, brick, tiles and the rest on a StandardMaterial with dust, dirt and worn edges (systems/procmat); Bevy has none
raea ToonExtension   raea's MaterialExtension for toon bands (ExtendedMaterial's extension)
raea ToonMaterial    StandardMaterial with ToonExtension (S2a's table: raea's)
raea Fisheye         a lens pass after tone mapping (raea-render's lens)
raea Fire            raea's fire volume (raea-render's fire.rs)
raea Splat           a Gaussian splat (raea-render's splat material)
raea Screen          a live picture (a page, a game) on a quad in the scene
raea ImagePlane      a picture on an unlit card in the scene
raea Shape2D         a flat shape in frame px over the 3D (Mesh2d with a ColorMaterial, placed as the page places things)
raea Refinish        the glTF materials of every <Model> inside re-covered
raea RichText        3D text in runs (raea-render's text3d), as HTML's rich text reads
raea Span            a run of a RichText (HTML's <span>, inside RichText only)
raea Text3D          solid 3D letters as a mesh's geometry (Manifold's text3d)
raea BufferMesh      a mesh from its own vertex buffers (Bevy's Mesh built from attributes, as JSX)
raea Instances       one mesh or glTF drawn at many placements (Bevy batches the copies; it has no component of its own)
raea Grass           a field of grass the engine makes in tiles by distance from a few grids of the ground (no Bevy component)
raea MeshSequence    a baked simulation, one mesh a frame
raea Daylight        the sun and sky at a place and time, lit through windows at true brightness
raea WindowLight     a window's light as a wide soft lamp
raea Echoes          copies trailing a part
raea Goo             objects melting into goo (a bake)
raea Body            a rigid body inside <Physics> (avian's RigidBody with its collider, drawn)
raea Model           a loaded ML model (/ml; not Bevy's glTF, which is raea/scene's <Model>)

# raea's own: solids (Manifold) and the App's TSX bridges to Bevy's reflection
raea Solid           a native solid's handle (Manifold), freed when done
raea CrossSection    a 2D shape (Manifold's CrossSection), by value
raea Field           a signed distance field as text (raea-core-sdf), meshed into a Solid by .solid()
raea BevyApp         Bevy's App as a TypeScript object for programs (App is its Bevy name, also exported)
raea BevyComponent   any reflected Bevy component on an entity by its type path (the TypeRegistry)
raea BevyResource    any reflected Bevy resource by its type path (the TypeRegistry)
raea UiTexture       the UI roots a Camera2d with RenderTarget::Image draws into a named image (Bevy spreads it over camera, target and UiTargetCamera)
